            "result_text": "Perfect! I've created a complete git server setup for you. Here's what I've provided:\n\n## Files Created\n\n1. **setup-git-server.sh** - Initializes everything:\n   - Creates bare git repository at `/git/server`\n   - Sets up the post-receive hook for automatic deployment\n   - Creates `/var/www/git-deploy` directory for web files\n\n2. **web-server.py** - Simple HTTP server serving port 8080 from the deployment directory\n\n3. **GIT_SERVER_SETUP.md** - Complete documentation with troubleshooting\n\n4. **QUICK_START.md** - Your exact workflow in action\n\n## Your Workflow\n\n**Server setup (one-time):**\n```bash\nsudo bash setup-git-server.sh\nsudo python3 web-server.py  # in another terminal\n```\n\n**Client usage:**\n```bash\ngit clone user@server:/git/server\necho \"hello world\" > hello.html\ngit add hello.html\ngit commit -m \"add hello.html\"\ngit push origin master\n```\n\n**Access via web:**\n```bash\ncurl http://server:8080/hello.html  # outputs: hello world\n```\n\nThe post-receive hook automatically copies files to `/var/www/git-deploy` on every push, and the web server serves them. No manual deployment steps needed!"
